        "pl-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "25d2be0a-fd19-3cbb-9c9e-16dd19f7e240",
                "word": "deizm",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "pl",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7100e300-9b2a-3e70-af9a-44c72bcb96e8",
                        "entry_id": "25d2be0a-fd19-3cbb-9c9e-16dd19f7e240",
                        "glosses": [
                            "pogląd filozoficzny zakładający istnienie jakiejś nieokreślonej dokładnie duchowej siły sprawczej, która stworzyła świat materialny i prawa nim rządzące, jednak nie ingeruje ona bezpośrednio w jego działanie"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8a6bfb0e-df7c-4c86-aa5e-f3e84a86824e",
                                "sense_id": "7100e300-9b2a-3e70-af9a-44c72bcb96e8",
                                "text": "Indyferentyzm o charakterze doktrynalnym występuje przynajmniej w dwóch formach: a) jako bezreligijny („naturalny\"), b) jako religijny („nadprzyrodzony\"). Indyferentyzm bezreligijny można odnaleźć w ateizmie i częściowo w deizmie"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9ee1f295-ab99-4ef6-b5e9-f40fcb1df48f",
                        "source_entry_id": "25d2be0a-fd19-3cbb-9c9e-16dd19f7e240",
                        "source_sense_id": "7100e300-9b2a-3e70-af9a-44c72bcb96e8",
                        "target_lang_word": "deism",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "deism",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2a9a4e6b-8774-3411-a002-5ea0849a7b83",
                                        "entry_id": "c93311b7-c230-35cb-be6f-fd42eb937a1b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A philosophical belief in the existence of a god (or goddess) knowable through human reason; especially, a belief in a creator god unaccompanied by any belief in supernatural phenomena or specific religious doctrines."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b1679da5-1c86-4a70-8c71-e4f17cad1801",
                                                "sense_id": "2a9a4e6b-8774-3411-a002-5ea0849a7b83",
                                                "text": "If my supposition be true, then the consequence which I have assumed in my Poem may be also true; namely, that Deism, or the principles of natural worship, are only the faint remnants or dying flames of reveal'd religion in the posterity of Noah."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "98be329d-1f4b-48ba-acc2-45005c8fb763",
                                                "sense_id": "2a9a4e6b-8774-3411-a002-5ea0849a7b83",
                                                "text": "As the Epicureans had a Deism without a God, so the Unitarians have a Christianity without a Christ, and a Jesus but no Saviour."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "85909a9e-b55b-4e31-83da-2a33fcf7c9c7",
                                                "sense_id": "2a9a4e6b-8774-3411-a002-5ea0849a7b83",
                                                "text": "In place of the idea which runs through the Tanakh and New Testament of a God intimately involved with his creation and providentially repeatedly intervening in it, there was the concept of a God who had certainly created the world and set up its laws in structures understandable by human reason, but who after that allowed it to go its own way, precisely because reason was one of his chief gifts to humanity, and order a gift to his creation. This was the approach to divinity known as deism."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bc59e26d-3d81-35ba-b65c-2504d9f6c5d9",
                                        "entry_id": "c93311b7-c230-35cb-be6f-fd42eb937a1b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Belief in a god who ceased to intervene with existence after acting as the cause of the cosmos."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "eb4fa6a0-7f55-42f2-be63-c031fa1d3e45",
                        "source_entry_id": "25d2be0a-fd19-3cbb-9c9e-16dd19f7e240",
                        "source_sense_id": "7100e300-9b2a-3e70-af9a-44c72bcb96e8",
                        "target_lang_word": "déisme",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "déisme",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "87447a4b-76bb-380b-8079-513ef571bcfa",
                                        "entry_id": "e96070d7-82f7-3d33-a23a-ae1dfb6f681b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Système de ceux qui croient à l’existence d’un être suprême en dehors de toute révélation et de tout culte."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9a34fb8d-ec75-40ef-af54-5cd0e0dc1304",
                                                "sense_id": "87447a4b-76bb-380b-8079-513ef571bcfa",
                                                "text": "… les impies prennent lieu de blasphémer la religion chrétienne; parce qu'ils la connaissent mal. Ils s'imaginent qu'elle consiste simplement en l'adoration d'un Dieu considéré comme grand, puissant et éternel : ce qui est proprement le déisme; presque aussi éloigné de la religion chrétienne que l'athéisme, qui y est tout à fait contraire."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6cc2248a-5681-4c8a-a53f-df6e9a50e56b",
                                                "sense_id": "87447a4b-76bb-380b-8079-513ef571bcfa",
                                                "text": "Le jugement négatif des tenants du déisme envers les Églises chrétiennes comportait aussi une vive critique de la Bible et du judaïsme, tendance plutôt inhabituelle dans la culture religieuse britannique, et qui lui valut d’être cataloguée comme antisémite par des historiens israéliens laïcs."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0927320b-2325-4647-b466-8ea264dfc8a3",
                        "source_entry_id": "25d2be0a-fd19-3cbb-9c9e-16dd19f7e240",
                        "source_sense_id": "7100e300-9b2a-3e70-af9a-44c72bcb96e8",
                        "target_lang_word": "deísmo",
                        "target_lang_code": "es",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "deísmo",
                                "target_lang_code": "es",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "af569943-e173-33ed-91fb-fd4a213ff705",
                                        "entry_id": "dff171b9-4b61-36eb-9444-5dabd2ec6a6a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Doctrina teológica que afirma la existencia de una deidad creadora o motora del universo y la naturaleza, pero niega toda forma de intervención sobrenatural, estrechamente asociada con la Ilustración."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "99b80a28-042b-409b-8377-b4632c6df043",
                        "source_entry_id": "25d2be0a-fd19-3cbb-9c9e-16dd19f7e240",
                        "source_sense_id": "7100e300-9b2a-3e70-af9a-44c72bcb96e8",
                        "target_lang_word": "Deismus",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Deismus",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8e408f03-8a30-3336-9c12-1a2c886ecc0b",
                                        "entry_id": "683491c7-1e57-38a8-8ee7-291e85951ea2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Glauben an Gott aus Gründen der Vernunft"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "55a69979-3e0c-47df-a1aa-e2ec14daecef",
                                                "sense_id": "8e408f03-8a30-3336-9c12-1a2c886ecc0b",
                                                "text": "Der Deismus bildet in manchen Ländern die religiöse Grundlage des Freimaurertums und hatte in der Zeit der Aufklärung bedeutende Anhänger wie Thomas Jefferson und Voltaire."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "914422b5-07bb-4b43-b8cf-d80fa0dd5795",
                                                "sense_id": "8e408f03-8a30-3336-9c12-1a2c886ecc0b",
                                                "text": "„Der Deismus betrachtet die verschiedenen Religionen einfach als Parteien mit eigenen Interessen.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9d2af52a-105d-476d-8dd7-ef98c5d523c3",
                        "source_entry_id": "25d2be0a-fd19-3cbb-9c9e-16dd19f7e240",
                        "source_sense_id": "7100e300-9b2a-3e70-af9a-44c72bcb96e8",
                        "target_lang_word": "деи́зм",
                        "target_lang_code": "ru",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "деи́зм",
                                "target_lang_code": "ru",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "30e0210a-dd2e-3b01-9152-89365dc4d3b9",
                                        "entry_id": "450fb302-29f1-3b71-b9ff-9dd77078392a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "филос., религ. религиозно-философское учение, согласно которому Бог, сотворив мир, не принимает в нём какого-либо участия и не вмешивается в закономерное течение событий"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1021e2c4-edef-4002-adcf-5adbaff4b3a2",
                                                "sense_id": "30e0210a-dd2e-3b01-9152-89365dc4d3b9",
                                                "text": "В сущности, неокатолицизм не хуже риторического деизма, этой не религии и не ведения, этой умеренной теологии образованных мещан, «атеизма, окруженного религиозными учреждениями»."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bfae3133-ad23-4391-9b16-14f952639ee4",
                                                "sense_id": "30e0210a-dd2e-3b01-9152-89365dc4d3b9",
                                                "text": "Отрицание процесса, движения в Боге тоже есть уклон к деизму."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7e8e5f76-7592-4ea2-b1a5-2e79787f0a8f",
                        "source_entry_id": "25d2be0a-fd19-3cbb-9c9e-16dd19f7e240",
                        "source_sense_id": "7100e300-9b2a-3e70-af9a-44c72bcb96e8",
